Say well done.

17
00:56:39.082 --> 00:56:40.082
You did it.

18
00:56:40.082 --> 00:56:41.082
You did it.

19
00:56:42.082 --> 00:56:43.082
You did it.

20
00:56:43.082 --> 00:56:44.082
Day 10.

21
00:56:46.082 --> 00:56:48.082
Say hi to each other one more time.

22
00:56:48.082 --> 00:56:49.082
You did it.

23
00:56:49.082 --> 00:56:50.082
Day 10.

24
00:56:50.082 --> 00:56:51.082
You are still livable.

25
00:56:52.082 --> 00:56:53.082
You are still alive.

26
00:56:54.082 --> 00:56:55.082
It is possible.

27
00:56:55.082 --> 00:56:56.082
It is possible.

28
00:56:57.082 --> 00:56:59.082
It is possible to go without anything.

29
00:56:59.082 --> 00:57:01.082
It is possible to go without anything.

30
00:57:01.082 --> 00:57:02.082
Thank you, Lord.

31
00:57:02.082 --> 00:57:03.082
Amen.

32
00:57:04.082 --> 00:57:06.082
We will go directly into the Word this morning.

33
00:57:06.082 --> 00:57:07.082
Hallelujah.

34
00:57:08.082 --> 00:57:10.082
It has been a powerful time.

35
00:57:13.082 --> 00:57:16.082
And I am sure we will hear testimonies.

36
00:57:17.082 --> 00:57:18.082
More and more.

37
00:57:18.082 --> 00:57:19.082
Amen.

38
00:57:22.082 --> 00:57:26.082
For the Lord uses it and we do not know how, that is mysterious.

39
00:57:28.082 --> 00:57:31.082
But He says if you do it, then you will receive a reward.

40
00:57:33.082 --> 00:57:36.082
And we want to go for everything the Lord has for us.

41
00:57:40.082 --> 00:57:42.082
And I want to elaborate on this.

42
00:57:42.082 --> 00:57:44.082
Two weeks ago I spoke about this.

43
00:57:53.082 --> 00:57:57.082
At that time I explained, I really want to teach about eternity this year.

44
00:57:57.082 --> 00:58:00.082
Or better said, our perspective on eternity.

45
00:58:06.082 --> 00:58:08.082
And I believe that the Lord wants to restore that.

46
00:58:18.082 --> 00:58:24.082
Because there is something in that eternal perspective that encourages us to make choices we otherwise would not make.

47
00:58:25.082 --> 00:58:27.082
And that is precisely the point.

48
00:58:37.082 --> 00:58:42.082
Jesus always pointed us to that eternity and urged us to look up.

49
00:58:42.082 --> 00:58:45.082
For He says it is about more than just this, this is not the end.

50
00:58:55.082 --> 00:59:00.082
And the apostles, the entire New Testament is full of it.

51
00:59:07.082 --> 00:59:16.082
And if you would not want to know anything about eternity and a reward in eternity, then you would have to throw out your entire New Testament.

52
00:59:17.082 --> 00:59:19.082
For it is everywhere.

53
00:59:20.082 --> 00:59:23.082
And what I mean by that is that we cannot ignore it.

54
00:59:29.082 --> 00:59:32.082
So I am excited to speak about this and see what the Lord does with it.

55
00:59:35.082 --> 00:59:37.082
And I want to start by saying a few things.

56
00:59:38.082 --> 00:59:39.082
Are you ready for this?

57
00:59:41.082 --> 00:59:42.082
Listen carefully to what follows.

58
00:59:43.082 --> 00:59:44.082
What is important?

59
00:59:46.082 --> 00:59:48.082
I want to let this word precede this.

60
00:59:50.082 --> 00:59:53.082
I am not talking about earning your salvation.

61
01:00:06.082 --> 01:00:14.082
And the Bible says if you believe in Jesus and what He has done, then you enter the kingdom.

62
01:00:16.082 --> 01:00:17.082
Let me put it this way.

63
01:00:19.082 --> 01:00:21.082
Your salvation is not a reward.

64
01:00:25.082 --> 01:00:28.082
I did not receive salvation as a reward, because I did nothing for it.

65
01:00:33.082 --> 01:00:35.082
That is why I love Jesus.

66
01:00:44.082 --> 01:00:45.082
But it is a gift.

67
01:00:46.082 --> 01:00:48.082
It is God's great gift to us.

68
01:01:02.082 --> 01:01:09.082
I love that. If you look at Ephesians 1 and 2, Paul speaks and he says, in Jesus and in Him.

69
01:01:10.082 --> 01:01:13.082
And then chapter 2 begins with, and as for you, you were dead.

70
01:01:16.082 --> 01:01:18.082
In other words, you had nothing to bring.

71
01:01:21.082 --> 01:01:23.082
You brought nothing, He brought everything.

72
01:01:26.082 --> 01:01:28.082
And to this day He is everything.

73
01:01:29.082 --> 01:01:33.082
So let me say, before everyone hears incorrectly what I am going to teach.

74
01:01:34.082 --> 01:01:36.082
I am not talking about your salvation.

75
01:01:37.082 --> 01:01:42.082
You have faith and that is the grace, the presumption of God to bring you into His kingdom.

76
01:01:50.082 --> 01:01:51.082
However.

77
01:01:52.082 --> 01:01:53.082
Say however.

78
01:01:54.082 --> 01:01:55.082
It does not end there.

79
01:01:59.082 --> 01:02:02.082
Your Bible is not very useful if we end there.

80
01:02:21.082 --> 01:02:25.082
I am talking about that same grace and that same faith that saved you.

81
01:02:26.082 --> 01:02:30.082
What gives you the strength to live in the kingdom as a disciple.

82
01:02:38.082 --> 01:02:42.082
For when you hear this kind of teaching, people become confused.

83
01:02:42.082 --> 01:02:48.082
And as soon as preachers, teachers, and others say things like we want to press into faith and abstinence.

84
01:02:49.082 --> 01:02:51.082
And all the things that Jesus has taught.

85
01:02:51.082 --> 01:02:53.082
People say wow, wait a minute.

86
01:03:02.082 --> 01:03:03.082
That is religious.

87
01:03:04.082 --> 01:03:05.082
That is religious.

88
01:03:06.082 --> 01:03:07.082
That is intense.

89
01:03:09.082 --> 01:03:10.082
That sounds like law, brother.

90
01:03:12.082 --> 01:03:14.082
And I am saved by grace, don't you know that?

91
01:03:19.082 --> 01:03:21.082
But then you have not understood your salvation.

92
01:03:24.082 --> 01:03:26.082
Then you have misunderstood faith and grace.

93
01:03:28.082 --> 01:03:29.082
For it does not end there.

94
01:03:34.082 --> 01:03:38.082
You were saved for something much greater than just being rescued from destruction.

95
01:03:43.082 --> 01:03:46.082
The story we believe has so much more glory in it.

96
01:03:57.082 --> 01:04:05.082
The same faith, and it all comes from the spirit, that same faith that enabled you to believe in your salvation.

97
01:04:08.082 --> 01:04:11.082
That is the same faith and the same grace.

98
01:04:13.082 --> 01:04:20.082
That you must use and that you must take up to follow me in that salvation.

99
01:04:26.082 --> 01:04:30.082
You will never find a verse in the Bible that says, be saved and then sit down.

100
01:04:30.082 --> 01:04:42.082
That just sounds wrong and yet we do that, somewhere in our walk we sit down.

101
01:04:47.082 --> 01:04:51.082
And when I say that, you say no of course not, but we actually do it.

102
01:04:55.082 --> 01:04:57.082
So it is not a contradiction.

103
01:05:01.082 --> 01:05:07.082
I was saved by grace through faith and now I live by faith through that grace in the kingdom.

104
01:05:11.082 --> 01:05:16.082
I was saved by grace through faith and now I live by faith through that grace in the kingdom.

105
01:05:21.082 --> 01:05:23.082
This is the introduction, are you following me so far?

106
01:05:24.082 --> 01:05:29.082
You might have thought we fasted so it would be a quick message, no way.

107
01:05:33.082 --> 01:05:38.082
He has given us everything to run with full dedication.

108
01:05:40.082 --> 01:05:42.082
And secondly this.

109
01:05:45.082 --> 01:05:49.082
This type of teaching carries weight with it.

110
01:05:49.082 --> 01:05:50.082
Always.

111
01:05:51.082 --> 01:05:52.082
And why is that?

112
01:05:53.082 --> 01:05:54.082
Because it is true.

113
01:05:57.082 --> 01:06:00.082
And when the truth is presented, you have two options.

114
01:06:03.082 --> 01:06:04.082
You can accept it.

115
01:06:08.082 --> 01:06:11.082
And start changing your life accordingly.

116
01:06:15.082 --> 01:06:18.082
Not just sitting and looking at it and thinking, okay it is good teaching.

117
01:06:20.082 --> 01:06:21.082
Nice preaching to me.

118
01:06:24.082 --> 01:06:26.082
I felt something, yes it was good.

119
01:06:41.082 --> 01:06:47.082
So you can accept it and start making daily choices, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday.

120
01:06:50.082 --> 01:06:52.082
To move yourself in that direction.

121
01:06:56.082 --> 01:06:59.082
And to begin receiving the reward for it.

122
01:07:02.082 --> 01:07:06.082
And the other option is that you hear it and reject it.

123
01:07:10.082 --> 01:07:12.082
And then you also do not receive the reward for it.

124
01:07:20.082 --> 01:07:24.082
And this is why I believe the Lord makes this clear time and again in the Bible.

125
01:07:25.082 --> 01:07:27.082
So that you cannot escape it.

126
01:07:28.082 --> 01:07:29.082
Thirdly.

127
01:07:30.082 --> 01:07:31.082
And then we dive into it.

128
01:07:40.082 --> 01:07:46.082
Thirdly, this is not a message that we take and then compete with each other.

129
01:07:49.082 --> 01:07:56.082
But we are talking about seeking the Lord in your life for the eternal reward that He has set for you.

130
01:08:04.082 --> 01:08:15.082
Paul said, I strive to take hold of that for which Christ took hold of me.

131
01:08:16.082 --> 01:08:18.082
Paul was running his race.

132
01:08:20.082 --> 01:08:22.082
Paul was running a race to win it.

133
01:08:25.082 --> 01:08:31.082
Having said that, so we don't look at each other, I can't say Laura, you and me, let's go, let's race for the reward.

134
01:08:32.082 --> 01:08:39.082
No, I have my own reward with Jesus that He set before the foundation of the earth.

135
01:08:40.082 --> 01:08:41.082
I mean, there's a reward before.

136
01:08:41.082 --> 01:08:44.082
So I can't tell someone else, come on, shall we do this together...

137
01:08:45.082 --> 01:08:51.082
No, because I am running for the race and the reward that Jesus has already prepared for me before creation.

138
01:08:53.082 --> 01:08:54.082
But...

139
01:08:55.082 --> 01:08:56.082
But...

140
01:08:59.082 --> 01:09:04.082
We are not in competition with each other for that one reward, because we each have our own.

141
01:09:07.082 --> 01:09:10.082
It is about your personal response to the Lord Jesus.

142
01:09:11.082 --> 01:09:18.082
Not only for the cross, but also how you have lived in your salvation for Him.

143
01:09:25.082 --> 01:09:30.082
But the Bible teaches in Hebrews that we may encourage one another in faith and good works.

144
01:09:31.082 --> 01:09:34.082
And it even says more so, as we see that day with a capital D approaching.

145
01:09:45.082 --> 01:09:47.082
And what is the day with a capital D?

146
01:09:48.082 --> 01:09:49.082
That is the day of judgment.

147
01:09:52.082 --> 01:09:54.082
When the Lord returns and comes in His glorious throne.

148
01:10:00.082 --> 01:10:03.082
So look at someone and say this sermon is completely for me.

149
01:10:09.082 --> 01:10:11.082
And I will make the right choice.

150
01:10:19.082 --> 01:10:22.082
If you have your Bible with you, look up 2 Corinthians 5.

151
01:10:30.082 --> 01:10:37.082
The judgment for believers is when Jesus as the ultimate judge gives a judgment on how you have lived.

152
01:10:53.082 --> 01:10:57.082
A final decision about the decisions you have made in your salvation.

153
01:11:01.082 --> 01:11:06.082
And let me tell you this. He is just looking forward to rewarding those who have been faithful.

154
01:11:11.082 --> 01:11:16.082
Jesus is not a judge who instills fear. He is beautiful and He is full of glory.

155
01:11:31.082 --> 01:11:42.082
And there will be no excuses to make at that moment. His eyes are full of fire, His hair is white as wool and He will judge justly as a judge.

156
01:11:46.082 --> 01:11:49.082
And that is a concept that is full of grace.

157
01:11:51.082 --> 01:11:53.082
And you might be thinking, how does that work then?

158
01:11:56.082 --> 01:11:59.082
And I will tell you this. He could have simply saved you.

159
01:12:01.082 --> 01:12:02.082
That's it.

160
01:12:03.082 --> 01:12:04.082
And that’s that.

161
01:12:08.082 --> 01:12:14.082
But he says now my son and daughter, I long to reward you for your faithfulness.

162
01:12:15.082 --> 01:12:16.082
How beautiful is that?

163
01:12:17.082 --> 01:12:18.082
He doesn't have to do that.

164
01:12:20.082 --> 01:12:23.082
Do you remember in Ephesus? It's all about him.

165
01:12:24.082 --> 01:12:25.082
He created everything.

166
01:12:26.082 --> 01:12:27.082
He made you.

167
01:12:28.082 --> 01:12:30.082
He gave you the gift that you have.

168
01:12:32.082 --> 01:12:35.082
He gave you the spirit to empower you.

169
01:12:37.082 --> 01:12:39.082
So it all starts with him.

170
01:12:41.082 --> 01:12:43.082
So why do we then receive a reward?

171
01:12:47.082 --> 01:12:51.082
Has anyone ever thought about that? Why do I actually receive a reward? I'm just happy that I am saved.

172
01:12:52.082 --> 01:12:53.082
It is gracious.

173
01:12:53.082 --> 01:12:54.082
Jesus is extravagant.

174
01:12:56.082 --> 01:12:57.082
Jesus is extravagant.

175
01:13:03.082 --> 01:13:10.082
When we say we want to worship him extravagantly, we don't realize that he always goes further than we do.

176
01:13:11.082 --> 01:13:19.082
So his glory, that is his goodness, is to restore us as sons and daughters in that glory.

177
01:13:32.082 --> 01:13:34.082
He has redeemed us back from Adam.

178
01:13:40.082 --> 01:13:43.082
And I truly believe that he can't wait for that day.

179
01:13:44.082 --> 01:13:49.082
He can't wait until those sons and daughters who have followed him by faith can receive a reward.

180
01:14:02.082 --> 01:14:04.082
He is so full of grace.

181
01:14:05.082 --> 01:14:08.082
And every small step we take in faith, He rewards.

182
01:14:18.082 --> 01:14:23.082
So the judgment on believers determines how we will live in the eternal kingdom.

183
01:14:28.082 --> 01:14:31.082
It determines our measure of responsibility.

184
01:14:35.082 --> 01:14:38.082
It determines our closeness to Jesus in the kingdom.

185
01:14:45.082 --> 01:14:51.082
Even the glory of your resurrection body is determined by acts of faith and faithfulness.

186
01:14:56.082 --> 01:14:59.082
Can we jump to Revelation 22 verse 12?

187
01:15:05.082 --> 01:15:12.082
And Jesus is speaking here and He says, I am coming soon.

188
01:15:15.082 --> 01:15:17.082
And I have the reward with me.

189
01:15:20.082 --> 01:15:23.082
And I will reward everyone.

190
01:15:25.082 --> 01:15:27.082
According to their deeds.

191
01:15:35.082 --> 01:15:39.082
So it is not bad to desire a reward.

192
01:15:39.082 --> 01:15:42.082
Jesus Himself taught about this.

193
01:15:46.082 --> 01:15:48.082
Second Corinthians 5.

194
01:15:49.082 --> 01:15:51.082
And Paul writes here.

195
01:15:51.082 --> 01:15:53.082
It is not comprehensive today.

196
01:15:53.082 --> 01:15:55.082
There is so much in the Bible about it.

197
01:15:55.082 --> 01:15:56.082
It is incredible.

198
01:15:56.082 --> 01:15:58.082
So I am not trying to be comprehensive.

199
01:15:58.082 --> 01:16:00.082
I am trying to give a few overviews.

200
01:16:09.082 --> 01:16:10.082
Paul writes this.

201
01:16:10.082 --> 01:16:13.082
First of all, for this true verse.

202
01:16:13.082 --> 01:16:15.082
He talks about the body.

203
01:16:15.082 --> 01:16:18.082
He talks about serving Christ as an apostle.

204
01:16:19.082 --> 01:16:25.082
And before this piece comes, Paul talks about his body.

205
01:16:30.082 --> 01:16:33.082
And how we wither away in the natural.

206
01:16:36.082 --> 01:16:39.082
And that in his ministry he has suffered for Christ.

207
01:16:42.082 --> 01:16:44.082
But he has an eternal need.

208
01:16:45.082 --> 01:16:47.082
For at the end of chapter 4 he says.

209
01:16:47.082 --> 01:16:50.082
But we live by faith and not by what we see.

210
01:17:00.082 --> 01:17:02.082
I do not look at that persecution.

211
01:17:02.082 --> 01:17:04.082
For in the light of eternity.

212
01:17:04.082 --> 01:17:06.082
That is what the Lord has prepared for me.

213
01:17:06.082 --> 01:17:08.082
And what the Lord has prepared for me.

214
01:17:08.082 --> 01:17:10.082
Is what the Lord has prepared for me.

215
01:17:10.082 --> 01:17:12.082
And what the Lord has prepared for me.

216
01:17:12.082 --> 01:17:15.082
But in eternity that is what the Lord has prepared for me.

217
01:17:15.082 --> 01:17:17.082
So much more beautiful than what is happening now.

218
01:17:20.082 --> 01:17:23.082
That does not mean that the persecution is light.

219
01:17:35.082 --> 01:17:38.082
But he says, when I think of that eternal house.

220
01:17:38.082 --> 01:17:43.082
This temporary suffering is nothing compared to that eternal glory.

221
01:17:45.082 --> 01:17:49.082
And for that, we need the Holy Spirit to have that vision.

222
01:17:57.082 --> 01:18:02.082
And he then says, therefore we take pride in doing what God wants.

223
01:18:03.082 --> 01:18:07.082
Both in this existence and in our existence with Him.

224
01:18:12.082 --> 01:18:15.082
For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ.

225
01:18:17.082 --> 01:18:28.082
So that each of us receives what he deserves for what he has done in his life.

226
01:18:29.082 --> 01:18:36.082
And then he elaborates further, whether it is good or bad.

227
01:18:38.082 --> 01:18:40.082
And he is addressing the church here.

228
01:18:44.082 --> 01:18:50.082
Paul reasons here because we know that the day of judgment will come.

229
01:18:51.082 --> 01:19:03.082
Therefore, we make it our goal to please the Lord only in our earthly body.

230
01:19:07.082 --> 01:19:10.082
And this is the first.

231
01:19:10.082 --> 01:19:16.082
Your goal in your salvation is to please the Lord, to bring pleasure to the Lord.

232
01:19:17.082 --> 01:19:19.082
It is as simple as that.

233
01:19:21.082 --> 01:19:23.082
It is to bring Him pleasure.

234
01:19:26.082 --> 01:19:30.082
The goal of salvation in my body is to please Him.

235
01:19:34.082 --> 01:19:38.082
The judgment reminds us that we are no longer our own.

236
01:19:39.082 --> 01:19:41.082
I belong to Jesus.

237
01:19:41.082 --> 01:19:46.082
Yes, I am a daughter, but I am also a servant.

238
01:19:49.082 --> 01:19:51.082
Yes, I am the bride, but I am also a servant.

239
01:19:52.082 --> 01:19:53.082
I am not God.

240
01:19:54.082 --> 01:19:55.082
I serve God.

241
01:19:56.082 --> 01:19:57.082
He does not serve me.

242
01:19:59.082 --> 01:20:00.082
He does not serve my will.

243
01:20:05.082 --> 01:20:09.082
Some things I will receive in this life and others I will receive in glory.

244
01:20:11.082 --> 01:20:13.082
This life is not about us.

245
01:20:20.082 --> 01:20:24.082
And if you then say, can I not just live how I want?

246
01:20:25.082 --> 01:20:26.082
No.

247
01:20:27.082 --> 01:20:29.082
The blood has bought you.

248
01:20:32.082 --> 01:20:35.082
And that word bought means that someone owns you.

249
01:20:37.082 --> 01:20:39.082
Let us return to the Word.

250
01:20:42.082 --> 01:20:46.082
The blood has redeemed you from hell, from death, from sin.

251
01:20:47.082 --> 01:20:48.082
And we can be glad about that.

252
01:20:51.082 --> 01:20:56.082
For if the whole Word is not preached anymore, then we take salvation far too lightly.

253
01:20:57.082 --> 01:21:02.082
If the Western church decides, yes, I do not want hell to be real, then we make salvation very easy.

254
01:21:07.082 --> 01:21:09.082
Who says you can teach that hell is not real?

255
01:21:11.082 --> 01:21:13.082
Who says you can teach that hell is not real?

256
01:21:17.082 --> 01:21:19.082
Who says you can teach that hell is not real?

257
01:21:20.082 --> 01:21:22.082
Who has made you god?

258
01:21:24.082 --> 01:21:26.082
Who says you can teach that hell is not real?

259
01:21:28.082 --> 01:21:29.082
How dare we?

260
01:21:34.082 --> 01:21:36.082
That is not our role.

261
01:21:40.082 --> 01:21:43.082
Then we make ourselves the judge over life and death, and we cannot do that.

262
01:21:50.082 --> 01:21:56.082
Jesus says, Vanessa, if you are ashamed of my Word, then you will be ashamed when you stand before that throne.

263
01:22:03.082 --> 01:22:09.082
And he does not make me a shame, but my actions will cause me to be ashamed in his presence.

264
01:22:20.082 --> 01:22:33.082
He is so pure and so full of love that when I stand before him, the shame I will feel is the shame I feel because I have not fully obeyed him.

265
01:22:34.082 --> 01:22:38.082
And how do I know that? I know that because there is no condemnation for those who are in Christ.

266
01:22:39.082 --> 01:22:48.082
But when I stand before him and I come to the realization that I have not fully taught what is in his Word, then I will be ashamed of that. Amen.

267
01:22:50.082 --> 01:22:51.082
It is intense, isn't it?

268
01:22:51.082 --> 01:22:54.082
And I stand here trembling as I bring it, but it is real.

269
01:23:01.082 --> 01:23:05.082
And that you are no longer your own means that you are no longer your own.

270
01:23:06.082 --> 01:23:10.082
And that means that you are no longer your own, that means that you are no longer your own.

271
01:23:10.082 --> 01:23:15.082
And that means that you are no longer your own, that means that your life has much more meaning to the Lord than we realize.

272
01:23:18.082 --> 01:23:21.082
He has bought you to be with him forever.

273
01:23:28.082 --> 01:23:33.082
And for the time that he places you, he places you in a family, so that you can do it together.

274
01:23:33.082 --> 01:23:35.082
In the body of Christ.

275
01:23:40.082 --> 01:23:45.082
A family, a body with many parts, but we belong together.

276
01:23:53.082 --> 01:23:57.082
So if you think, I can do what I want, then you are actually a family.

277
01:23:58.082 --> 01:24:01.082
So if you think, I can do what I want, then you are actually a family.

278
01:24:06.082 --> 01:24:11.082
So if you think, I can just do whatever I feel like, then you are damaging the body of Christ.

279
01:24:13.082 --> 01:24:15.082
Why? Because your sin matters.

280
01:24:16.082 --> 01:24:18.082
You do not only affect yourself.

281
01:24:19.082 --> 01:24:20.082
That is nonsense.

282
01:24:21.082 --> 01:24:22.082
And you know it.

283
01:24:22.082 --> 01:24:28.082
It affects everyone you are connected to.

284
01:24:32.082 --> 01:24:35.082
And it has consequences beyond just this life.

285
01:24:37.082 --> 01:24:38.082
It comes before the judgment.

286
01:24:45.082 --> 01:24:50.082
Where the man with eyes of fire says, son or daughter, this is what I have to say about your life.

287
01:24:53.082 --> 01:24:56.082
John said, he is full of grace and truth.

288
01:25:02.082 --> 01:25:05.082
You will not make a fool of him on that day.

289
01:25:07.082 --> 01:25:09.082
There are no excuses for that throne.

290
01:25:11.082 --> 01:25:14.082
He will weigh it justly.

291
01:25:23.082 --> 01:25:29.082
So Paul understood that there was a responsibility entrusted to him by the Lord.

292
01:25:33.082 --> 01:25:37.082
And he taught it to the church and it is the same for every believer.

293
01:25:42.082 --> 01:25:43.082
I have so much.

294
01:25:46.082 --> 01:25:49.082
The throne of judgment concerns two things.

295
01:25:53.082 --> 01:25:57.082
Receiving the reward for the good you have done with your life.

296
01:26:04.082 --> 01:26:08.082
And the second is the loss you experience from the bad you have done in your body.

297
01:26:14.082 --> 01:26:17.082
So that reward is compensation.

298
01:26:22.082 --> 01:26:44.082
Paul speaks about compensating and that brings us back to the teaching of Jesus, where Jesus says, what you have lost, you will receive back again.

299
01:26:45.082 --> 01:26:53.082
So that compensating, that means in Greek to receive back.

300
01:26:56.082 --> 01:26:59.082
That which already belonged to me.

301
01:27:01.082 --> 01:27:02.082
But that which is lost is done.

302
01:27:03.082 --> 01:27:04.082
Or given up.

303
01:27:04.082 --> 01:27:18.082
And Jesus says, give your life now and you will receive so much more in return.

304
01:27:35.082 --> 01:27:36.082
Sorry.

305
01:27:37.082 --> 01:27:41.082
He says, it will all come back.

306
01:27:44.082 --> 01:27:47.082
Matthew 19, verse 28, so Jesus and the Word.

307
01:27:54.082 --> 01:27:56.082
And Jesus is saying this here to the disciples.

308
01:27:57.082 --> 01:28:04.082
And He says, I assure you, in other words, you can count on this.

309
01:28:07.082 --> 01:28:10.082
When the time comes that everything will be renewed.

310
01:28:13.082 --> 01:28:17.082
When the Son of Man will sit in His majesty on His throne.

311
01:28:21.082 --> 01:28:25.082
You who have followed me will also sit on the twelve thrones.

312
01:28:27.082 --> 01:28:29.082
He is speaking here to the twelve disciples.

313
01:28:32.082 --> 01:28:37.082
And He is already giving them a vision for their reward that is tied to their following Him.

314
01:28:40.082 --> 01:28:42.082
Most of them will literally lose their heads.

315
01:28:49.082 --> 01:28:51.082
They will all die a martyr's death.

316
01:28:57.082 --> 01:29:03.082
And before this happens, Jesus says, I want you to look up, I want you to see that glory.

317
01:29:06.082 --> 01:29:09.082
Yes, it will be costly to follow me.

318
01:29:11.082 --> 01:29:13.082
But you will be richly rewarded.

319
01:29:20.082 --> 01:29:24.082
They will speak rightly about the twelve tribes of Israel and that is a reward.

320
01:29:25.082 --> 01:29:27.082
That is not just anything.

321
01:29:38.082 --> 01:29:43.082
Think about this. You who are placed on a throne, why? Because you have followed Him.

322
01:29:43.082 --> 01:29:56.082
We can hardly rule over our own lives, and then we will rule on thrones over nations and angels.

323
01:29:59.082 --> 01:30:01.082
It is all based on faith and on faithfulness.

324
01:30:04.082 --> 01:30:05.082
And everyone.

325
01:30:08.082 --> 01:30:11.082
And each one. He opens it up here for everyone.

326
01:30:14.082 --> 01:30:15.082
And everyone.

327
01:30:20.082 --> 01:30:22.082
Who has left things behind.

328
01:30:26.082 --> 01:30:32.082
And then he says, brothers, sisters, father, mother, children, houses, whoever has left these for my name's sake.

329
01:30:36.082 --> 01:30:37.082
Will receive.

330
01:30:40.082 --> 01:30:41.082
A hundredfold.

331
01:30:43.082 --> 01:30:53.082
And you can read that and then think to yourself, well, I don't know what to make of that, but it is true.

332
01:30:57.082 --> 01:31:00.082
And you will receive eternal life.

333
01:31:07.082 --> 01:31:11.082
So everything the Lord asks you to give up is not lost.

334
01:31:14.082 --> 01:31:17.082
It is stored up until the renewal of all things.

335
01:31:27.082 --> 01:31:34.082
And He wants to give you a reward that goes beyond what you have had to leave behind in this life and in this time.

336
01:31:34.082 --> 01:31:35.082
Okay.

337
01:31:40.082 --> 01:31:42.082
That which you have done good in the body.

338
01:31:45.082 --> 01:31:47.082
And that is the Greek word for good.

339
01:31:50.082 --> 01:31:53.082
And that means that which finds its origin in God.

340
01:31:56.082 --> 01:31:58.082
And is confirmed by Him in faith.

341
01:32:00.082 --> 01:32:01.082
It is all faith.

342
01:32:04.082 --> 01:32:06.082
Whatever we do in faith.

343
01:32:07.082 --> 01:32:08.082
To follow Him.

344
01:32:12.082 --> 01:32:15.082
Whatever He asks of you in which you must trust Him.

345
01:32:21.082 --> 01:32:25.082
That is empowered by the Spirit and that is something good that you have done in your body.

346
01:32:26.082 --> 01:32:32.082
And Jesus says, you will be helped to do that faithful act by my Spirit.

347
01:32:42.082 --> 01:32:46.082
And that brings us back to Matthew 6. When you fast, there is a reward attached to it.

348
01:32:49.082 --> 01:32:53.082
When you fast, you will receive a reward.

349
01:32:56.082 --> 01:32:58.082
And I will reward that faithfulness.

350
01:33:05.082 --> 01:33:11.082
How do we know that we are engaged in faith by the Spirit, because you would never make that choice with your own flesh?

351
01:33:11.082 --> 01:33:18.082
You would never choose to do those things yourself, unless you feel that God encourages you to do this.

352
01:33:28.082 --> 01:33:30.082
It is a sacrificial life.

353
01:33:34.082 --> 01:33:36.082
And that is faith and the power of God at work in you.

354
01:33:42.082 --> 01:33:48.082
And you find all of that in Matthew 6, when he talks about prayers and fasting and serving. It is all through faith.

355
01:33:57.082 --> 01:34:04.082
And the Lord says the judgment, that which you have done for me in faithfulness,

356
01:34:05.082 --> 01:34:07.082
I will openly reward on that day.

357
01:34:15.082 --> 01:34:18.082
And that will be a testimony that you have with me for all eternity.

358
01:34:24.082 --> 01:34:28.082
Your testimony, your story with God here on earth, lives forever.

359
01:34:29.082 --> 01:34:32.082
How do you know that, Vanessa? Read Hebrews 11.

360
01:34:49.082 --> 01:34:56.082
Read those stories of the heroes of faith and then you will see that it is stored up, that it is recorded.

361
01:34:57.082 --> 01:35:03.082
And in their earthly life, they have not received everything, but that reward is there in the kingdom.

362
01:35:09.082 --> 01:35:14.082
It is good to pursue a good testimony that has eternal value.

363
01:35:17.082 --> 01:35:18.082
Finally.

364
01:35:21.082 --> 01:35:23.082
Loss, the bad you have done in the body.

365
01:35:27.082 --> 01:35:31.082
And this is also Paul here in 1 Corinthians 3, verses 10 to 15.

366
01:35:41.082 --> 01:35:49.082
And he says, by the grace that God has given me, I have laid a foundation as a skilled master builder.

367
01:35:57.082 --> 01:36:03.082
And he is talking about the ministry, about building the church.

368
01:36:03.082 --> 01:36:09.082
And he says, listen, I have built the foundation, Christ and him crucified, that is the basis.

369
01:36:17.082 --> 01:36:24.082
And that applies to your life as well. Christ and him crucified, that is the basis, that is the foundation on which you build your house.

370
01:36:27.082 --> 01:36:36.082
And others build upon it, and no one can lay another foundation than Jesus.

371
01:36:44.082 --> 01:36:50.082
If anyone builds on this foundation with gold, silver, wood, and straw,

372
01:36:57.082 --> 01:37:03.082
then it will be made clear what their work is worth.

373
01:37:06.082 --> 01:37:13.082
For on that day, with a capital D, on that day of judgment, it will be revealed.

374
01:37:16.082 --> 01:37:18.082
Through fire, it will be brought to light.

375
01:37:20.082 --> 01:37:23.082
What are his eyes made of?

376
01:37:27.082 --> 01:37:37.082
Your life, how you have built after your salvation, his eyes that are full of fire look right through it.

377
01:37:40.082 --> 01:37:41.082
Completely transparent.

378
01:37:43.082 --> 01:37:45.082
And that is already the case, by the way.

379
01:37:47.082 --> 01:37:48.082
It is already the case.

380
01:37:48.082 --> 01:37:55.082
But what it means that on that day you will have nothing more to say, this is how your life was for the years.

381
01:38:11.082 --> 01:38:17.082
There is no moment for discussion, where you sit down together at the table and spend a few hours debating why this or why that.

382
01:38:19.082 --> 01:38:22.082
That is not your place, He is the King.

383
01:38:25.082 --> 01:38:26.082
He is the Judge.

384
01:38:29.082 --> 01:38:31.082
And He cannot be put to shame.

385
01:38:38.082 --> 01:38:43.082
Nothing is hidden from His eyes, to whom we all must give account.

386
01:38:48.082 --> 01:38:53.082
And for a believer, this is the most sobering verse you can find.

387
01:39:01.082 --> 01:39:05.082
And then He goes on and says, when someone's building stands firm.

388
01:39:09.082 --> 01:39:12.082
In other words, that which goes into eternity.

389
01:39:12.082 --> 01:39:25.082
Then the builder, you therefore, I, will be rewarded.

390
01:39:28.082 --> 01:39:31.082
And when is that? If it can withstand the fire.

391
01:39:33.082 --> 01:39:34.082
If it is burned up.

392
01:39:34.082 --> 01:39:42.082
If it is burned up, then the builder will pay a price for that.

393
01:39:45.082 --> 01:39:47.082
And maybe you are thinking now, is this really in my Bible?

394
01:39:52.082 --> 01:39:55.082
On that day of judgment, you will experience loss.

395
01:39:58.082 --> 01:39:59.082
You will be saved.

396
01:40:05.082 --> 01:40:11.082
Your foundation stands. You believed in Christ, so you are saved.

397
01:40:11.082 --> 01:40:13.082
But you have built nothing upon it.

398
01:40:17.082 --> 01:40:20.082
You have given Him nothing that brought honor to His name.

399
01:40:27.082 --> 01:40:29.082
He wants to reward everyone, but He cannot.

400
01:40:29.082 --> 01:40:34.082
He can only do that if you have done things that are worthy of reward.

401
01:40:35.082 --> 01:40:37.082
He longs for it, he wants that.

402
01:40:38.082 --> 01:40:40.082
You are saved, you are in.

403
01:40:45.082 --> 01:40:49.082
But how much do we want to please the Lord in our body?

404
01:40:53.082 --> 01:40:55.082
We want to give him glory on that day.

405
01:40:59.082 --> 01:41:03.082
The Bible says, live a life that honors his name.

406
01:41:06.082 --> 01:41:08.082
You are saved, he has set you free.

407
01:41:10.082 --> 01:41:11.082
Is he not worth everything?

408
01:41:13.082 --> 01:41:14.082
Is he not beautiful?

409
01:41:15.082 --> 01:41:16.082
Is he not gracious?

410
01:41:18.082 --> 01:41:19.082
Is he not kind?

411
01:41:19.082 --> 01:41:21.082
I don't know, because I can lose.

412
01:41:21.082 --> 01:41:25.082
But if you walk with him in faith and happiness, then you will receive a reward.

413
01:41:35.082 --> 01:41:36.082
It is still a kingdom.

414
01:41:38.082 --> 01:41:40.082
It is not our life, our little life, that we want.

415
01:41:41.082 --> 01:41:43.082
With Jesus. That is not the gospel.

416
01:41:43.082 --> 01:41:46.082
The gospel is that you are welcomed into a kingdom, where there is a king.

417
01:41:49.082 --> 01:41:54.082
And I do what I want for Jesus, but we are saved in a kingdom that has a king.

418
01:41:58.082 --> 01:42:03.082
And this carries weight, because it is up to us to respond to this.

419
01:42:03.082 --> 01:42:05.082
But it is glorious, it is good.

420
01:42:05.082 --> 01:42:09.082
It is a good God who wants to give you your holiness.

421
01:42:09.082 --> 01:42:12.082
Give yourself, revalue with Him eternally.

422
01:42:22.082 --> 01:42:23.082
Let us dance.

423
01:42:34.082 --> 01:42:42.082
If the Western church makes it too much of a personal thing, then we live our own little lives for ourselves.

424
01:42:42.082 --> 01:42:45.082
And we no longer live it under Christ, the King.

425
01:42:53.082 --> 01:42:58.082
And we feel justified in doing what He has clearly said.

426
01:42:58.082 --> 01:43:00.082
This is not the way to work with me.

427
01:43:04.082 --> 01:43:07.082
But He has the best for us, in all things.

428
01:43:12.082 --> 01:43:15.082
The frightening part is falling outside.

429
01:43:15.082 --> 01:43:17.082
To fall outside of holiness.

430
01:43:17.082 --> 01:43:21.082
Holiness is given to urge you to live fully for Him.

431
01:43:27.082 --> 01:43:29.082
Lord, we thank You for Your Word.

432
01:43:29.082 --> 01:43:32.082
And I want to thank You that it is real and that it is true.

433
01:43:36.082 --> 01:43:37.082
And through Your Spirit,

434
01:43:40.082 --> 01:43:42.082
we walk in more faithfulness.

435
01:43:45.082 --> 01:43:46.082
For Your glory.

436
01:43:47.082 --> 01:43:48.082
For it is all about You.

437
01:43:50.082 --> 01:43:51.082
My life is not for myself.

438
01:43:53.082 --> 01:43:55.082
I am introduced by the blood.

439
01:43:55.082 --> 01:43:56.082
My life is not for myself.

440
01:43:58.082 --> 01:44:00.082
I am bought by the blood.

441
01:44:08.082 --> 01:44:11.082
And you do not only want to heal me, you want more than that.

442
01:44:11.082 --> 01:44:15.082
You long for me to live in glory, in glorious ways.

443
01:44:25.082 --> 01:44:26.082
The Lord is good.

444
01:44:29.082 --> 01:44:30.082
The Lord is good.

445
01:44:42.082 --> 01:44:44.082
Lord, give us the right perspective.

446
01:44:48.082 --> 01:44:50.082
That this is a glorious reality.

447
01:44:52.082 --> 01:44:54.082
And that you are good and kind.

448
01:44:56.082 --> 01:44:58.082
That you are good and kind.

449
01:45:03.082 --> 01:45:04.082
Sing it.

450
01:45:20.082 --> 01:45:21.082
Sing it.

451
01:45:25.082 --> 01:45:28.082
You are holy.

452
01:45:55.082 --> 01:45:57.082
Hallelujah.

453
01:46:04.082 --> 01:46:06.082
You are beautiful.

454
01:46:26.082 --> 01:46:30.082
Come, let me see your face, Lord.

455
01:46:35.082 --> 01:46:38.082
Your strength and your wrath.

456
01:46:44.082 --> 01:46:47.082
I know that I will make it to the end.

457
01:46:50.082 --> 01:46:52.082
If I can see your face.

458
01:46:56.082 --> 01:46:59.082
Can we all close our eyes?

459
01:47:04.082 --> 01:47:08.082
I have two invitations for all of us.

460
01:47:09.082 --> 01:47:12.082
I want to earnestly ask if you would close your eyes...

461
01:47:12.082 --> 01:47:15.082
so that you can focus on you and you alone.

462
01:47:20.082 --> 01:47:23.082
My first invitation is very simple.

463
01:47:23.082 --> 01:47:26.082
Vanessa has clearly taught...

464
01:47:26.082 --> 01:47:31.082
and in her preface, in her introduction to this sermon...

465
01:47:31.082 --> 01:47:35.082
she has clearly stated and explained so well...

466
01:47:35.082 --> 01:47:40.082
that there is salvation and a wonderful life...

467
01:47:40.082 --> 01:47:43.082
of abundance and rewards...

468
01:47:43.082 --> 01:47:50.082
if we truly decide to live for God's kingdom after our salvation.

469
01:47:50.082 --> 01:47:55.082
But I want to talk about our salvation in this first invitation.

470
01:47:56.082 --> 01:48:00.082
And I know that today there are a number of people who have come to church...

471
01:48:00.082 --> 01:48:07.082
for whom this applies to make a choice for Jesus today.

472
01:48:07.082 --> 01:48:12.082
Soon we will talk about the life you have in that salvation.

473
01:48:12.082 --> 01:48:17.082
But I want to talk now, while all eyes are closed, about salvation itself.

474
01:48:17.082 --> 01:48:19.082
My question is...

475
01:48:19.082 --> 01:48:24.082
have you received Jesus into your own life?

476
01:48:24.082 --> 01:48:28.082
Have you received Jesus as your personal God...

477
01:48:28.082 --> 01:48:32.082
your Lord, your Redeemer, and your very best friend?

478
01:48:32.082 --> 01:48:35.082
And it is important that all eyes are closed...

479
01:48:35.082 --> 01:48:37.082
so that you can look into your own soul...

480
01:48:37.082 --> 01:48:41.082
and not look around at what other people think of you...

481
01:48:41.082 --> 01:48:44.082
or that your father or mother might be watching...

482
01:48:44.082 --> 01:48:47.082
Johnny, Peter, now it's time for you to give yourself.

483
01:48:47.082 --> 01:48:50.082
No, this is entirely for you and you alone.

484
01:48:50.082 --> 01:48:55.082
Have you accepted Jesus so that you know you are saved?

485
01:48:55.082 --> 01:48:57.082
What if tomorrow is your last day?

486
01:48:57.082 --> 01:48:59.082
What if today is your last day?

487
01:48:59.082 --> 01:49:03.082
Do you know that you can stand face to face...

488
01:49:03.082 --> 01:49:06.082
with the Most High who can judge you.

489
01:49:06.082 --> 01:49:09.082
He who has the right to judge your life.

490
01:49:09.082 --> 01:49:12.082
When you see Him face to face...

491
01:49:12.082 --> 01:49:15.082
do you know that you are saved and that He says...

